CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*symbol '__c11_atomic.*' is unknown$
--
Regression for the Clang __c11_atomic_* intrinsic declarations in
clang_builtin_headers.h.  These are generated by Clang for libc++'s
<atomic> on macOS and must be parseable by CBMC.

Taking the address of each intrinsic pins down that the declaration
is visible in user scope without actually calling the stub (which
would trigger "no body for callee" failures).
